# Development Workflow & Quality Standards

## **PNPM Monorepo Commands**
Always use PNPM commands instead of direct Docker/npm commands:

### **Development Environment**
```bash
# Full-stack development
pnpm run dev                    # All services (frontend + backend)
pnpm run setup:dev             # One-command complete setup

# Focused development  
pnpm run dev:frontend          # Frontend-only (UI developers)
pnpm run dev:backend           # Backend-only (API developers)
pnpm run setup:frontend        # Frontend-focused setup
pnpm run setup:backend         # Backend-focused setup
```

### **Service Management**
```bash
# Logs by category
pnpm run logs                   # All services
pnpm run logs:frontend         # Frontend logs only
pnpm run logs:backend          # Backend logs only

# Logs by service
pnpm run logs:auth             # Auth service
pnpm run logs:user             # User service
pnpm run logs:api              # API Gateway

# Health checks
pnpm run health                # Backend API health
pnpm run health:frontend       # Frontend health
```

## **Git Workflow with Husky**
Pre-commit hooks are configured in [.husky/](mdc:.husky/):

### **Smart Linting (lint-staged)**
- **Frontend files**: ESLint + TypeScript + Prettier
- **Backend files**: ESLint + Prettier
- **Config files**: Prettier formatting only
- **Prisma schemas**: Auto-formatting

### **Commit Standards** 
[commitlint.config.js](mdc:commitlint.config.js) enforces conventional commits:
```bash
# Commit types
feat: new feature
fix: bug fix
docs: documentation changes
style: code formatting
refactor: code refactoring
perf: performance improvements
test: adding tests
build: build system changes
ci: CI/CD changes
chore: maintenance tasks

# Examples
git commit -m "feat(auth): add 2FA support"
git commit -m "fix(api): resolve CORS issue"
git commit -m "docs: update setup guide"

# Interactive commit helper
pnpm run commit
```

### **Pre-push Hooks**
Configured in [.husky/pre-push](mdc:.husky/pre-push):
1. Run all workspace tests
2. TypeScript type checking
3. Build verification
4. Only pushes if all checks pass

## **Quality Standards**
Configured in [package.json](mdc:package.json) lint-staged section:

```json
{
  "lint-staged": {
    "frontend/**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}": [
      "pnpm --filter frontend run lint:fix",
      "pnpm --filter frontend run type-check",
      "prettier --write"
    ],
    "backend/**/*.{js,ts}": [
      "eslint --fix",
      "prettier --write"
    ],
    "**/*.prisma": [
      "prettier --write"
    ]
  }
}
```

## **Documentation Strategy**
- **[memory-bank/](mdc:memory-bank/)**: Project intelligence and context
- **[docs/](mdc:docs/)**: Technical documentation and guides
- **[wiki/](mdc:wiki/)**: Quick start and overview content
- **README files**: Service-specific setup instructions

## **Docker Optimization**
Multiple Docker Compose configurations:
- [docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker-compose.yml) - Full development environment
- [docker-compose.frontend.yml](mdc:docker-compose.frontend.yml) - Frontend-only
- [docker-compose.backend.yml](mdc:docker-compose.backend.yml) - Backend-only

Dockerignore files optimize builds:
- [.dockerignore](mdc:.dockerignore) - General exclusions
- [.dockerignore.backend](mdc:.dockerignore.backend) - Backend-specific
- [.dockerignore.frontend](mdc:.dockerignore.frontend) - Frontend-specific

## **Testing Strategy**
```bash
# Run all tests
pnpm run test

# Service-specific tests
docker-compose exec auth-service pnpm test
docker-compose exec frontend pnpm test

# Test with coverage
pnpm run test:coverage
```